-- import: bling.fifthtry.site/note

-- ds.page: Error Handling

`fastn` considers `404.ftd` and `500.ftd` in your fastn project folder as
special files.

If a fastn package contains a `404.ftd` file then visiting any 404 route (a
route that does not exist) will render this 404.ftd file.

For any other fastn error (error in syntax, calls to http processor failing
etc), the 500.ftd in current fastn package will be rendered.

When env `DEBUG` is set, the original error with a nicer message is shown
instead to give the developer some more context. In production, the `fastn
--trace serve` output should be considered around these 404/500 requests to
know more about the cause.

-- end: ds.page
